    "body": "Work landed locally on issue/67-cross-drill-spindle (0610e2b), gating now:\n- New `operation/cross_spindle.rs`: cross_drill shifts the holes into the spindle frame by the work-offset origin, measures the bar radius about that line, runs the drilling kernel unchanged, shifts back; on-origin parts skip the shift (bit-identical paths).\n- Measured on an r10 bar at (10,4) under a moved G54 (radii from G54): start 15.770 -> 15.000, hop 26.4/32.4/46.4 -> 21.213, clearance 35.770 -> 15.000 (now the same as the bar on the origin).\n- The spindle law (#62) now covers a mill-turn Drill with cross holes too: a bar 10.770 mm off an unmoved G54 used to drill silently; now refused by name at generation and posting.\n- On a plain lathe, a part the axis fit can't read as turned is refused by name (the comment promised it; now true). A mill-turn still drills square/hex bars (normal cross-drill stock), with clearance measured about the posted spindle.\n- Tests (fail on main): drilling_cross_spindle::{a_cross_drill_off_the_world_origin_under_a_moved_g54_drills_the_on_origin_chain, a_cross_drill_on_a_bar_off_an_unmoved_work_offset_is_refused_by_name, a_lathe_cross_drill_on_a_part_that_reads_as_no_revolve_is_refused_by_name}.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
